1
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:07,407
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:09,877 --> 00:00:11,311
Hm.

3
00:00:11,311 --> 00:00:13,647
I could just burn this place down.

4
00:00:13,647 --> 00:00:16,049
There was a lot of junk at
the bottom of the stairs;

5
00:00:16,049 --> 00:00:18,552
I could start a fire there,
everybody comes running:

6
00:00:18,552 --> 00:00:19,620
"AAAAH!"

7
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:22,189
then I could loot the building
while they're putting it out.

8
00:00:22,189 --> 00:00:24,191
Wait, I'm getting ahead of myself.

9
00:00:24,191 --> 00:00:29,096
My situation's only maybe hopeless,
not set-fire-to-everything hopeless.

10
00:00:29,096 --> 00:00:30,464
Hello, neighbor!

11
00:00:31,231 --> 00:00:34,434
Look at you. You're like
a magical white rabbit.

12
00:00:34,434 --> 00:00:37,104
If you run away from me, that
means I should follow you, right?

13
00:00:38,071 --> 00:00:42,175
Oh, I know THAT look. That's
the look of wisdom right there.

14
00:00:42,175 --> 00:00:43,977
You've seen things.

15
00:00:43,977 --> 00:00:45,345
Well, I have, too.

16
00:00:45,345 --> 00:00:46,480
What are you drinking?

17
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:47,347
MAN #1: Was that you knocking?

18
00:00:47,347 --> 00:00:48,649
No, this is me rocking.

19
00:00:48,649 --> 00:00:50,384
MAN #1: I didn't know we still had a door.

20
00:00:50,384 --> 00:00:52,486
The door to your mind, man.

21
00:00:52,486 --> 00:00:54,154
Dammit, I know you have the answers,

22
00:00:54,154 --> 00:00:56,957
but I don't want to seem too
eager. That wouldn't be cool.

23
00:00:56,957 --> 00:00:59,760
Well at least somebody's on
the path to enlightenment.

24
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:01,728
MAN #2: Oh. I thought you were a cop.

25
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:02,496
Freeze!

26
00:01:02,496 --> 00:01:03,430
WOMAN #1: He's one of us.

27
00:01:03,430 --> 00:01:05,933
Uh--yes, I am.

28
00:01:05,933 --> 00:01:08,402
WOMAN #1: I told you they'd
be coming for us next.

29
00:01:08,402 --> 00:01:09,970
MAN #2: Just this once I hope you're wrong.

30
00:01:10,837 --> 00:01:11,905
Oh.

31
00:01:11,905 --> 00:01:16,376
I should leave. Something's up here.
I don't want any guilt by association.

32
00:01:16,376 --> 00:01:18,645
These people are running
a commune or something

33
00:01:18,645 --> 00:01:21,848
where they don't think anything of
a stranger walking into their home.

34
00:01:21,848 --> 00:01:23,517
WOMAN #2: I can't take it anymore.

35
00:01:23,517 --> 00:01:24,651
MAN #3: Everything's going to be okay.

36
00:01:24,651 --> 00:01:26,720
Oop, trouble in paradise.

37
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:30,390
Yeah, this has "not gonna
last" written all over it.

38
00:01:30,390 --> 00:01:34,561
Hm. It's either a commune or
an open house with bad timing,

39
00:01:34,561 --> 00:01:36,763
but I doubt that. That lady
didn't look like a realtor.

40
00:01:36,763 --> 00:01:38,966
MAN #4: Psst! Hey you! In here!

41
00:01:38,966 --> 00:01:41,001
Sure. You got any drugs?

42
00:01:41,001 --> 00:01:42,269
You look like the type.
MAN #4: Head for the roof!

43
00:01:42,269 --> 00:01:43,904
I don't have any--
MAN #4: There's no time to lose!

44
00:01:43,904 --> 00:01:44,671
Yeah...

45
00:01:44,671 --> 00:01:46,073
MAN #5: HERE THEY COME! HELP!

46
00:01:46,073 --> 00:01:49,376
Hey, you know what? When people are
screaming and running one direction,

47
00:01:49,376 --> 00:01:51,311
I find it's best to just not question that

48
00:01:51,311 --> 00:01:53,614
and assume they have more
current information than I do.

49
00:01:53,614 --> 00:01:55,182
I don't like learning things the hard way--

50
00:01:55,182 --> 00:01:56,116
MAN #4: Get in here, quick!

51
00:01:56,717 --> 00:01:58,218
MAN #4: Keep moving! Head for the roof!

52
00:01:58,218 --> 00:02:00,854
--but I love letting other
people learn the hard way for me.

53
00:02:00,854 --> 00:02:02,022
[gunshots]

54
00:02:02,022 --> 00:02:04,658
Oh, shit! Those were gunshots!

55
00:02:04,658 --> 00:02:06,793
I knew this place was bad news.

56
00:02:06,793 --> 00:02:09,162
Those people obviously
have their own problems

57
00:02:09,162 --> 00:02:10,831
and I'm going to let them keep them.

58
00:02:10,831 --> 00:02:12,199
That's a big building.

59
00:02:12,733 --> 00:02:14,101
WHOA!

60
00:02:14,101 --> 00:02:16,203
Jesus! They're shooting at me!

61
00:02:16,203 --> 00:02:18,205
Okay, let's see you chase me here.

62
00:02:18,905 --> 00:02:21,041
Oh boy... oh boy...

63
00:02:21,041 --> 00:02:23,243
Gravity still doesn't love me.

64
00:02:23,243 --> 00:02:25,379
Or rather, it loves me too much.

65
00:02:25,379 --> 00:02:26,747
[gunshot]
OH MY GOD!

66
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:29,783
NO! GET OUT OF HERE!

67
00:02:29,783 --> 00:02:30,884
I HATE YOU!

68
00:02:30,884 --> 00:02:32,452
Aah! Aa-aah!

69
00:02:32,452 --> 00:02:36,390
This is the second-worst day of
my life! Or maybe third-worst!

70
00:02:36,390 --> 00:02:37,891
[gunshots]
FUCK!

71
00:02:37,891 --> 00:02:39,826
Oh, this is something! I'll take it.

72
00:02:39,826 --> 00:02:43,430
Okay... that's one cause
of death off the list.

73
00:02:43,430 --> 00:02:44,431
WOOP!

74
00:02:44,431 --> 00:02:45,732
SPLINTERS!

75
00:02:45,732 --> 00:02:47,034
BLAGH!

76
00:02:48,635 --> 00:02:49,770
No-NO!

77
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:50,904
Not this!

78
00:02:50,904 --> 00:02:51,738
NRAAAGH!

79
00:02:51,738 --> 00:02:52,606
[shudders]

80
00:02:52,873 --> 00:02:53,373
[shudders]

81
00:02:58,445 --> 00:03:01,815
[groaning]
Owwww-hoo-hoo-owww...

82
00:03:01,815 --> 00:03:03,583
ALYX: Dr. Freeman, I presume?

83
00:03:03,583 --> 00:03:06,086
You a nurse? I need morphine!

84
00:03:06,086 --> 00:03:07,688
ALYX: You'd better hurry.

85
00:03:07,688 --> 00:03:12,592
Owww-how-how-hoowwwww...

86
00:03:12,592 --> 00:03:15,195
Fuck's going on here?

87
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:15,729
ALYX: Dr. Kleiner said--

88
00:03:15,729 --> 00:03:18,198
Hey, we should get their guns.

89
00:03:18,198 --> 00:03:18,932
ALYX: I don't think it occurred--

90
00:03:18,932 --> 00:03:22,969
They're not here. They don't
even have their stun prods.

91
00:03:22,969 --> 00:03:26,239
She must've collected them and
thrown them out the window.

92
00:03:26,239 --> 00:03:27,908
Why did she do that?

93
00:03:27,908 --> 00:03:30,710
How did she take down a room full of cops?

94
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:35,182
Must've been an explosive,
huh? A nail bomb or something.

95
00:03:35,182 --> 00:03:39,419
You know, where I come from, killing
cops means they send a lot more cops.

96
00:03:39,419 --> 00:03:43,023
ALYX: I'm Alyx Vance. My father
worked with you back in Black Mesa?

97
00:03:43,023 --> 00:03:43,790
Oh.

98
00:03:43,790 --> 00:03:45,559
ALYX: I'm sure you don't
remember me, though.

99
00:03:45,559 --> 00:03:48,261
I'm not sure I remember your father.

100
00:03:48,261 --> 00:03:50,097
ALYX: Man of few words, aren't you?

101
00:03:50,097 --> 00:03:52,032
Listen, smart-ass. I don't--

102
00:03:52,032 --> 00:03:54,634
Oh, okay. Well fuck you then.

103
00:03:54,634 --> 00:03:58,338
Yeah, I talk a lot, but that's
because I GET THINGS DONE!

104
00:03:58,338 --> 00:04:01,108
ALYX: Remember him from Black Mesa?
Your old administrator.

105
00:04:01,108 --> 00:04:02,309
No?

106
00:04:02,309 --> 00:04:04,244
ALYX: Don't get my dad started on Dr. Breen.

107
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:07,514
There were hundreds of people
with doctorates at Black Mesa.

108
00:04:07,514 --> 00:04:08,248
ALYX: Through here.

109
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:09,683
Are we being watched?

110
00:04:09,683 --> 00:04:11,685
Did you check behind those barrels?

111
00:04:11,685 --> 00:04:14,020
What's with this "Get Smart" shit?

112
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:17,257
[humming Get Smart theme]

113
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:19,659
ALYX: Funny you showing up
on this day in particular.

114
00:04:19,659 --> 00:04:29,469
[humming Get Smart theme]

115
00:04:29,469 --> 00:04:31,671
ALYX: We've been helping
people escape the city on foot.

116
00:04:31,671 --> 00:04:33,340
Why'd you jump that? There's stairs here.

117
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:35,709
ALYX: It's a dangerous route to my
father's lab, through the old canals?

118
00:04:35,709 --> 00:04:37,844
That's bad for your knees. I know.

119
00:04:37,844 --> 00:04:40,514
ALYX: Today, we're finally on
the verge of having a better way.

120
00:04:40,514 --> 00:04:42,482
You're just jumping for no reason.

121
00:04:42,482 --> 00:04:43,116
All right.

122
00:04:43,116 --> 00:04:45,652
ALYX: Heh. Here. Let me buy you a drink.

123
00:04:45,652 --> 00:04:49,322
That is a GREAT idea. You're a good nurse.

124
00:04:49,322 --> 00:04:52,425
Oh. You meant the vending machine.

125
00:04:52,425 --> 00:04:53,527
ALYX: Oh, and by the way.

126
00:04:53,527 --> 00:04:54,361
Ah.

127
00:04:54,361 --> 00:04:55,595
ALYX: Nice to finally meet you.

128
00:04:55,595 --> 00:04:57,130
Sure is!

129
00:04:57,130 --> 00:05:01,134
Okay, time to go see the
chief. You can wait outside.

130
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:04,738
Hm! Nice setup! Yeah, those
tanks could hold full bodies.

131
00:05:04,738 --> 00:05:06,973
KLEINER: Blast that little--
Where did she get to?

132
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:09,142
I'm just going to act like
I've been here the whole time.

133
00:05:09,142 --> 00:05:10,010
KLEINER: Lamarr! Come out of there!

134
00:05:10,010 --> 00:05:10,544
Oh, what...?

135
00:05:10,544 --> 00:05:12,045
ALYX: Uh-oh. Everything
all right, Dr. Kleiner?

136
00:05:12,045 --> 00:05:13,780
You're ruining everything!

137
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:17,784
KLEINER: Well, almost all right. Lamarr
has gotten out of her crate again.

138
00:05:17,784 --> 00:05:19,886
Don't make him explain himself!

139
00:05:19,886 --> 00:05:21,822
KLEINER: ...I'd suspect
Barney of trapping and--

140
00:05:21,822 --> 00:05:23,089
Just leave!

141
00:05:23,089 --> 00:05:25,058
KLEINER: Goodness! Gordon Freeman!

142
00:05:25,058 --> 00:05:25,892
Ha-hey!

143
00:05:25,892 --> 00:05:27,160
KLEINER: It really is you, isn't it?

144
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:31,031
ALYX: I found him wandering around
outside. Bit of a troublemaker, isn't he?

145
00:05:31,031 --> 00:05:31,665
Oh!

146
00:05:31,665 --> 00:05:33,533
KLEINER: We owe a great deal to Dr. Freeman.

147
00:05:33,533 --> 00:05:34,834
GOD DAMN RIGHT!

148
00:05:34,834 --> 00:05:36,736
KLEINER: Even though trouble
does tend to follow in his wake.

149
00:05:36,736 --> 00:05:39,739
That's a good way of
putting it. It follows ME.

150
00:05:39,739 --> 00:05:42,976
KLEINER: I must say, Gordon, you've
come at a very opportune time.

151
00:05:42,976 --> 00:05:43,577
Ah!

152
00:05:43,577 --> 00:05:47,647
KLEINER: Alyx has just installed the
final piece for our resurrected teleport.

153
00:05:47,647 --> 00:05:49,716
ALYX: I can't take any credit
for the breakthrough, doctor.

154
00:05:49,716 --> 00:05:52,719
KLEINER: Nonsense. Your talents
surpass your loveliness.

155
00:05:52,719 --> 00:05:54,788
ALYX: Let's just see if
this thing works, okay?

156
00:05:54,788 --> 00:05:55,789
BARNEY: Well, is he here?

157
00:05:55,789 --> 00:05:58,058
Are those doors still open?

158
00:05:58,058 --> 00:06:00,260
BARNEY: Man, Gordon.
You've stirred up the hive!

159
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:03,763
Yeah, I bet! She killed five cops!
They're going to smoke this place.

160
00:06:03,763 --> 00:06:06,866
BARNEY: We can't keep him here long, doc.
It'll jeopardize everything we've worked for.

161
00:06:06,866 --> 00:06:08,535
ALYX: Don't worry. He's coming with me.

162
00:06:08,535 --> 00:06:10,403
No, you SHOULD worry! This--

163
00:06:10,403 --> 00:06:11,705
KLEINER: This is a red letter day.

164
00:06:11,705 --> 00:06:12,305
Ehh...

165
00:06:12,305 --> 00:06:15,208
KLEINER: We'll inaugurate the new
teleport with a double transmission.

166
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:16,142
What's that on her hip?

167
00:06:16,142 --> 00:06:18,545
BARNEY: You mean it's
working? For real this time?

168
00:06:18,545 --> 00:06:21,381
BARNEY: Because, I still have
nightmares about that cat.

169
00:06:21,381 --> 00:06:23,617
KLEINER: Now now, there's
nothing to be nervous about.

170
00:06:23,617 --> 00:06:24,184
ALYX: What cat?

171
00:06:24,184 --> 00:06:27,888
KLEINER: We've made major strides
since then. Major strides.

172
00:06:27,888 --> 00:06:28,588
ALYX: What cat?

173
00:06:28,588 --> 00:06:31,992
Are you thick? He obviously
killed a cat in an experiment.

174
00:06:31,992 --> 00:06:33,927
You people don't know Kleiner.

175
00:06:33,927 --> 00:06:38,598
KLEINER: Oh dear, you're right. I almost
forgot. Barney, I'll give you the honor.

176
00:06:38,598 --> 00:06:40,934
BARNEY: I've gotta get back on my shift--

177
00:06:40,934 --> 00:06:44,037
Yeah! You gotta go
find that cop-killer, huh?

178
00:06:44,037 --> 00:06:46,139
Man, I'm getting a bad vibe here.

179
00:06:46,139 --> 00:06:49,242
I was hoping Kleiner and I could
get back to doing some real science,

180
00:06:49,242 --> 00:06:51,578
but now I think there's so
much heat, my whole future's--

181
00:06:51,578 --> 00:06:52,212
AAH!

182
00:06:53,246 --> 00:06:57,250
Kleiner, this is dark.
But your lab, your rules.

183
00:06:57,250 --> 00:07:00,420
If you want to kill your assistant,
I'm not going to stop you.

184
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:05,625
KLEINER: Certainly not! Never fear, Gordon.
She's de-beaked and completely harmless.

185
00:07:05,625 --> 00:07:06,926
OR IS IT?

186
00:07:06,926 --> 00:07:11,331
KLEINER: The worst she might do is attempt
to couple with your head... fruitlessly.

187
00:07:11,331 --> 00:07:13,133
BARNEY: Get that thing away from me!

188
00:07:13,133 --> 00:07:14,067
KLEINER: Here, my pet.

189
00:07:14,067 --> 00:07:16,102
The years have not been kind, huh?

190
00:07:16,102 --> 00:07:19,406
KLEINER: No, not up there! No, no!

191
00:07:19,406 --> 00:07:22,709
KLEINER: Careful, Lamarr!
Those are quite fragile!

192
00:07:22,709 --> 00:07:26,413
KLEINER: Oh, fie! It'll be another week
before I can coax her out of there.

193
00:07:26,413 --> 00:07:29,015
How many people HAVE you killed, Kleiner?

194
00:07:29,015 --> 00:07:32,152
ALYX: Hah, Barney, you're
not an animal-person.

195
00:07:32,152 --> 00:07:35,855
You know, I thought he was the dumb
one, but you're as green as they come!

196
00:07:35,855 --> 00:07:38,425
You know they mind-rape you, right?

197
00:07:38,425 --> 00:07:40,827
You're like this little bobble toy here.

198
00:07:40,827 --> 00:07:43,263
You're going to learn things the hard way.

199
00:07:43,263 --> 00:07:46,232
Oh no. He wants me to put that on?

200
00:07:46,232 --> 00:07:49,869
Kleiner, I've got a lot of
bad memories with those suits.

201
00:07:49,869 --> 00:07:50,970
Can we...?

202
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:53,039
Oh no. He's giving me the look.

203
00:07:53,039 --> 00:07:55,675
I'd better do what he says.
I know that look.

204
00:07:55,675 --> 00:08:01,715
I think I'm the only person here who realizes
just how dangerous Kleiner actually is.

205
00:08:01,715 --> 00:08:03,116
Grah...

206
00:08:03,116 --> 00:08:06,219
Yep. These hands are made for strangling...

207
00:08:06,219 --> 00:08:06,753
...and theorems.

208
00:08:06,753 --> 00:08:11,157
KLEINER: Well, Gordon, I see your HEV
suit still fits you like a glove...

209
00:08:11,157 --> 00:08:12,726
KLEINER: ...at least the glove parts do.

210
00:08:12,726 --> 00:08:13,660
It IS tight.

211
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:18,231
KLEINER: I've made a few modifications but
I'll just acquaint you with the essentials.

212
00:08:18,231 --> 00:08:19,032
KLEINER: Now, let's see.

213
00:08:19,032 --> 00:08:22,569
I think I AM more buff. The
invasion was a marathon!

214
00:08:22,569 --> 00:08:25,105
KLEINER: "The Mark V
Hazardous Environment Suit

215
00:08:25,105 --> 00:08:27,640
KLEINER: "has been redesigned
for comfort and utility."

216
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:28,842
Hey, what about the helmet?

217
00:08:28,842 --> 00:08:29,743
[distant alarms]
KLEINER: Oh, dear.

218
00:08:29,743 --> 00:08:31,277
[distant alarms]
BARNEY: Doc, we don't have time for this!

219
00:08:31,277 --> 00:08:32,345
[distant alarms]
See, this is what I mean.

220
00:08:32,345 --> 00:08:34,314
BARNEY: At least get that
suit juiced up, Gordon.

221
00:08:34,314 --> 00:08:36,549
KLEINER: Good idea. There's
a charger on the wall.

222
00:08:36,549 --> 00:08:40,020
Oh, so I can turn on that
voice again? No, I'm good.

223
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:43,923
KLEINER: I've modified your suit to
draw power from Combine energy outlets

224
00:08:43,923 --> 00:08:46,192
KLEINER: which are plentiful
wherever THEY patrol.

225
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:48,595
"They"... That's the Tripods, right?

226
00:08:48,595 --> 00:08:50,463
ALYX: Meanwhile, let's
get this show on the road.

227
00:08:50,463 --> 00:08:51,664
Shut up.

228
00:08:51,664 --> 00:08:53,900
Yeah, this place is
going to get raided soon,

229
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:57,637
but I'm not worried about
Kleiner. He's a survivor like me.

230
00:08:57,637 --> 00:09:02,242
Yeah, look at that. I bet I haven't
seen half of his bag of tricks.

231
00:09:02,242 --> 00:09:04,044
He probably just has to hit two switches

232
00:09:04,044 --> 00:09:06,780
and his printer will
transform into a shotgun.

233
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:07,547
OOF!

234
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:11,718
That prick's doing that on
purpose. I'll deal with him later.

235
00:09:11,718 --> 00:09:13,753
Hey, that's me in the photo!

236
00:09:13,753 --> 00:09:17,157
I don't even remember
taking this. Was I high?

237
00:09:17,157 --> 00:09:20,193
Okay, that guy next to
Kleiner looks familiar...

238
00:09:20,193 --> 00:09:22,996
and there are a lot of
the Einstein-hair guys...

239
00:09:22,996 --> 00:09:25,331
...I don't recognize anyone else here.

240
00:09:25,331 --> 00:09:28,535
Why does this look like
it was taken in the 1800s?

241
00:09:28,535 --> 00:09:31,971
What's going on?! Is this
an alternate reality?

242
00:09:31,971 --> 00:09:34,541
I've been hopping across
space and time here...

243
00:09:35,875 --> 00:09:39,212
Oh, this should be good. We're
going to have some REAL fun.

244
00:09:39,212 --> 00:09:42,749
KLEINER: Gordon, why don't you position
yourself near the panel over there

245
00:09:42,749 --> 00:09:44,117
KLEINER: and wait for my word?

246
00:09:44,117 --> 00:09:45,552
With pleasure!
ELI: Izzy, are you there?

247
00:09:45,552 --> 00:09:49,355
KLEINER: Yes, yes, Eli. Bit
of a hold up on this end.

248
00:09:49,355 --> 00:09:52,192
KLEINER: You'll never guess who found
his way into our lab this morning.

249
00:09:52,192 --> 00:09:53,960
Harvard, huh?

250
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:55,328
ELI: That's not who I think it is, is it?

251
00:09:55,328 --> 00:09:56,162
Behold!

252
00:09:56,162 --> 00:09:59,899
KLEINER: Indeed it is. And it's our
intention to send him packing straightaway

253
00:09:59,899 --> 00:10:01,734
KLEINER: in the company
of your lovely daughter.

254
00:10:01,734 --> 00:10:04,137
"We've come for your daughter, Chuck."

255
00:10:04,137 --> 00:10:05,738
ELI: We're all set on this end.

256
00:10:05,738 --> 00:10:06,940
ALYX: Then let's do it.

257
00:10:07,807 --> 00:10:08,208
KLEINER: Let's see.

258
00:10:08,208 --> 00:10:12,078
Ha ha ha. You're going to get a show here.

259
00:10:12,078 --> 00:10:14,447
KLEINER: ...parameters to
CY base and LG orbifold...

260
00:10:14,447 --> 00:10:15,782
This is so sweet.

261
00:10:15,782 --> 00:10:19,419
KLEINER: ...Hilbert inclusive.
Conditions could hardly be more ideal.

262
00:10:19,419 --> 00:10:20,120
Amazing.

263
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:22,188
BARNEY: That's what you said last time.

264
00:10:22,188 --> 00:10:23,656
ALYX: Hey, yeah. About that cat?

265
00:10:23,656 --> 00:10:26,092
Yeah, you might die.
KLEINER: Initializing in 3... 2. .. 1!

266
00:10:26,092 --> 00:10:28,128
2... 1!
KLEINER: Initializing in 3... 2... 1!

267
00:10:29,329 --> 00:10:32,832
Awww...
KLEINER: Oh, fiddlesticks. What now?

268
00:10:32,832 --> 00:10:35,568
Man...
ALYX: Uh, doctor? The plug.

269
00:10:35,568 --> 00:10:37,837
KLEINER: Dear me. You're right.

270
00:10:37,837 --> 00:10:40,240
KLEINER: Gordon, would
you mind plugging us in?

271
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,841
Not in the slightest!

272
00:10:41,841 --> 00:10:42,609
ALYX: It's right there, Gordon.

273
00:10:42,609 --> 00:10:45,945
You realize that the voltage is so
high to blow the plug out of the wall,

274
00:10:45,945 --> 00:10:47,881
this can't be close to stable.

275
00:10:47,881 --> 00:10:49,516
OH! LOOK AT THAT ARCING!

276
00:10:50,316 --> 00:10:51,818
KLEINER: Excellent.

277
00:10:51,818 --> 00:10:53,386
ALYX: You're going to let
Gordon throw the switch?

278
00:10:53,386 --> 00:10:54,954
Certainly!

279
00:10:54,954 --> 00:10:57,023
KLEINER: Gordon? Go right ahead.

280
00:10:57,023 --> 00:10:58,725
Hahaha.

281
00:10:58,725 --> 00:11:01,427
This is going to be like one of
those dunking booths at the fair,

282
00:11:01,427 --> 00:11:05,598
except instead of dunking you in water,
you're going to get dunked out of existence.

283
00:11:05,598 --> 00:11:06,933
BARNEY: I can't look!

284
00:11:06,933 --> 00:11:08,301
ALYX: Uh...

285
00:11:08,301 --> 00:11:09,602
Come on!

286
00:11:09,602 --> 00:11:10,470
ALYX: Ooookay...

287
00:11:10,470 --> 00:11:11,704
Come on, come on!

288
00:11:11,704 --> 00:11:13,339
ALYX: OoooooOOOOOOOHHHH--!

289
00:11:13,339 --> 00:11:14,474
YES!
ALYX: OoooooOOOOOOOHHHH--!

290
00:11:15,375 --> 00:11:20,446
That was beautiful! This is
what it's all about right here.

291
00:11:20,446 --> 00:11:22,415
Kleiner, you have any champagne?

292
00:11:22,415 --> 00:11:24,417
KLEINER: Well? Did it work?

293
00:11:24,417 --> 00:11:26,219
ELI: See for yourself.

294
00:11:26,219 --> 00:11:26,886
ALYX: Hey, doc!

295
00:11:26,886 --> 00:11:27,754
Oh, bonus.

296
00:11:27,754 --> 00:11:31,891
KLEINER: Thank goodness. My
relief is almost palpable.

297
00:11:31,891 --> 00:11:33,159
ELI: Fantastic work, Izzy.

298
00:11:33,159 --> 00:11:33,793
It is.

299
00:11:33,793 --> 00:11:38,431
KLEINER: Well, I can't take all the credit.
Dr. Freeman proved an able assistant.

300
00:11:38,431 --> 00:11:39,332
Kleiner humor.

301
00:11:39,332 --> 00:11:40,934
ELI: Let's go ahead and
bring Gordon through now.

302
00:11:40,934 --> 00:11:43,937
KLEINER: Right you are. Speak
to you again in a few moments.

303
00:11:43,937 --> 00:11:46,339
BARNEY: Good job, Gordon,
throwing that switch and all?

304
00:11:46,339 --> 00:11:49,442
BARNEY: I can see your MIT
education really pays for itself.

305
00:11:49,442 --> 00:11:51,811
And what are you?! A middle-aged
high school dropout?!

306
00:11:51,811 --> 00:11:52,912
BARNEY: Gee, thanks.

307
00:11:52,912 --> 00:11:56,816
KLEINER: Gordon, as soon as you're
in position, we'll send you to Eli's.

308
00:11:56,816 --> 00:11:58,418
[distant alarms]
BARNEY: And not a moment too soon.

309
00:11:58,418 --> 00:12:02,055
I'M A DOCTOR, SHITMUNCH!
MY RESEARCH WENT INTO THIS!

310
00:12:02,055 --> 00:12:03,723
Not that you'd understand!

311
00:12:03,723 --> 00:12:07,226
If I find a dog toy for you to chew
on, I'll be sure to bring it to you!

312
00:12:07,226 --> 00:12:09,295
Taking shit from a guard...

313
00:12:09,295 --> 00:12:11,264
No wonder Kleiner doesn't mind killing you.

314
00:12:11,264 --> 00:12:16,803
KLEINER: Excellent.
Initializing in 3... 2... 1.

315
00:12:16,803 --> 00:12:19,339
Hey, this one's not green.

316
00:12:19,339 --> 00:12:20,707
BARNEY: Good luck out there, Gordon.

317
00:12:20,707 --> 00:12:24,110
Yeah, you'd BETTER try
to get on my good side.

318
00:12:24,110 --> 00:12:27,780
KLEINER: Bon voyage, and best of
luck in your future endeavors.

319
00:12:27,780 --> 00:12:28,915
Oh, I'll be back.

320
00:12:30,183 --> 00:12:32,585
Ah, I knew it. Shut it down...

321
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:34,287
BARNEY: It's your pet,
the freaking headhumper!

322
00:12:34,287 --> 00:12:36,556
Hey! The current's off! SHUT IT DOWN!

323
00:12:37,824 --> 00:12:40,193
Oh no! Not again!

324
00:12:40,193 --> 00:12:43,329
SHUT IT DOWN! THIS IS
BLACK MESA ALL OVER AGAIN!

325
00:12:43,329 --> 00:12:44,097
ALYX: He's coming through, dad.

326
00:12:44,097 --> 00:12:47,700
Oh my god, BEHIND YOU! WHAT'S BEHIND YOU?!

327
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:49,802
IT'S RIGHT THERE! STOP IT!

328
00:12:49,802 --> 00:12:51,571
MOSSMAN: Something's drawing him away.

329
00:12:51,571 --> 00:12:52,438
Oh god!

330
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:54,641
BREEN: What's the meaning
of this? Who ARE you?!

331
00:12:54,641 --> 00:12:55,508
Who are YOU?!

332
00:12:55,508 --> 00:12:56,476
BREEN: How did you get in here?

333
00:12:56,476 --> 00:12:57,410
I DON'T KNOW!

334
00:12:58,611 --> 00:13:01,648
KLEINER, SHUT IT DOWN! JUST SHUT IT DOWN!

335
00:13:01,648 --> 00:13:04,584
IT'S GOING TO SEND ME BACK
TO THAT ALIEN WORLD AGAIN!

336
00:13:04,584 --> 00:13:09,455
YOU CAN'T DO THIS TO ME, KLEINER! DON'T
SEND ME BACK THERE! I CAN'T GO BACK!

337
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:10,156
ALYX: There he is!

338
00:13:10,156 --> 00:13:12,091
IT'S STILL THERE! KILL IT!

339
00:13:13,259 --> 00:13:14,227
BREEN: I'm all but certain it was...

340
00:13:14,227 --> 00:13:15,795
RAAH!

341
00:13:15,795 --> 00:13:17,330
BREEN: ...Gordon Freeman.

342
00:13:17,330 --> 00:13:18,398
WHUH!

343
00:13:18,398 --> 00:13:19,699
[underwater panicking]

344
00:13:20,833 --> 00:13:21,968
[underwater panicking]

